    "ninjo": "To see the rigid hierarchy that keeps the common people suffering finally brought low. Kunimichi has witnessed too much injustice perpetuated by the celestial order - peasants starving while nobles feast, talented individuals held back by birth, and the Emperor's divine mandate used to justify cruelty. He longs for a world where merit and compassion matter more than bloodline and divine favor. This desire constantly puts him at odds with his official duties, as he must publicly support the very system he secretly works to undermine.",
